-E (optical drive speed): send SET STREAMING through SG_IO.

set_dvdspeed() hands the SET STREAMING packet to the drive with the
CDROM_SEND_PACKET request.  On LikeOS an optical drive (/dev/sr0) takes any
packet command through SG_IO instead, so the LikeOS branch sends the same
command and parameter list that way; the function body is unchanged.  If it
fails, hdparm falls back to CDROM_SELECT_SPEED as before (which the LikeOS
kernel does not answer, so the result is the usual "both failed" message).

